{{Short description|Small reef in the Egyptian Red Sea}}
[[File:Elphinstone Reef.jpg|thumb|right|Elphinstone Reef]]
'''Elphinstone Reef''' (also known as '''Sha'ab Abu Hamra''') is a standalone [[reef]] in the [[Egypt]]ian [[Red Sea]] situated about 30 kilometers north from [[Marsa Alam|the town of Marsa Alam in Egypt]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.marsaalam.com/Elphinstone_Reef.html|title=Elphinstone Reef|publisher=}}</ref> The [[coral]] community in this reef is primarily composed of soft corals such as ''[[Dendronephthya]]'' species.<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Riegl|first1=B.|last2=Piller|first2=W. E.|title=Coral frameworks revisited–reefs and coral carpets in the northern Red Sea|journal=Coral Reefs|language=en|volume=18|issue=3|pages=241–253|doi=10.1007/s003380050188|issn=0722-4028|year=1999|s2cid=16931660 |url=http://doc.rero.ch/record/16318/files/PAL_E917.pdf }}</ref>

